Recorded excerpts from the observed pre-fix R 4.6.1 devtools runs.
These are concise excerpts, not full console transcripts.

All stages used this wrapper and test filter:
bash attic/cnf_verify3/review_semantics/run_r46.sh -e 'devtools::test(filter = "^CnfInputs$", stop_on_failure = TRUE)'
The initial run additionally set options(testthat.progress.max_fails = Inf).

Original constructors, initial regression file:
[ FAIL 24 | WARN 0 | SKIP 0 | PASS 56 ]
Confirmed accepted dimensional/classed inputs, accepted invalid text,
unchanged Latin-1 encoding marks, and the C-CTYPE native escape collision.

First constructor correction, new native-byte regression:
[ FAIL 4 | WARN 0 | SKIP 0 | PASS 87 ]
Unmarked 0xFF under C CTYPE was accepted as a name/domain/atom value and
enc2utf8() substituted literal ASCII "<ff>". An invalid name created an
environment binding. validEnc() alone returned TRUE.

Before strict native-byte validation and before the universe getter change:
11 failing checks, 89 passing checks before testthat stopped at its failure limit.
Four checks were the native-byte failures above. Seven getter failures/errors
showed retained Latin-1/native marks, accepted matrix/classed queries, accepted
UTF-8/Latin-1 aliases of ASCII native escapes under C, and invalid native text
reaching ordinary lookup instead of validation.
